 "how_to_replay": {
  "expect": "Counts drift upward between snapshots as new markets settle — that is why every rate here is stamped with the window it was measured over. Two snapshots are only comparable through their windows.",
  "source": "UMA official Polygon Optimistic Oracle V2 subgraph (public endpoint, in `coverage.source`)",
  "steps": [
   "Page optimisticPriceRequests filtered to the three canonical Polymarket requester adapters in `coverage.canonical_requesters`, state:Settled.",
   "Group requests by the market_id carried in the decoded ancillary data; multiple oracle rounds on one market collapse to one row.",
   "Rebuild each market's rule template with `rule_feature_definitions`: lowercase `title\\n description`, substring-match every needle, join the active feature names with '+', or 'plain' when none fire.",
   "A market counts as disputed when its request carries a disputer.",
   "proposal_changed compares settlementPrice against proposedPrice, excluding the TOO_EARLY sentinel on either side."
  ]
 },
